.patch lang_pl
.title "Polish UI: sound and demo names, menus, buttons, headers and dialogs (needs polish_font)"
.requires polish_font

; Translation of the user interface. Image texts are drawn at build time with our own pixel font
; (nuxdsp/pixfont.py): ".draw IMAGE at X Y W H" clears that rectangle of the image and centres the
; text in it, so frames and icons stay as they are. Accents go in the row above the letters and
; ogonki in the row below. Image numbers: docs/FIRMWARE_MAP.md. Names and menu values are
; laid out anew in the space of their pointer tables (".table"), so a name may grow when others
; shrink. Strings use Unicode; polish_font draws the Polish letters.

